  "Poet and essayist; the author of 'The New Colossus', the sonnet inscribed on the Statue of Liberty, and the first American poet of the Jewish immigrant.",
  "Born Emma Lazarus in New York on 22 July 1849 into a wealthy Sephardi Jewish family; she published her first book at seventeen and was encouraged by Emerson. In the 1880s the Russian pogroms turned her into a Zionist and a campaigner for the Jewish refugees, producing Songs of a Semite (1882) and The Dance to Death (1882), and 'The New Colossus' (1883) for the Bartholdi Pedestal Fund. She died in New York on 19 November 1887, aged thirty-eight.",
